                <pb facs="0363" n="353" xml:id="pg353"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1200: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-13T23:00:00-03:00">November 13, 1937—11
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>162. My 155, November 12, 2 p.m. In informal conversation with the President this
                    afternoon I stressed harmful effects of suspending foreign debt payments in the
                    United States. Boucas tells me tonight very confidentially that the President
                    has just authorized the December payments on the dollar bonds.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
